WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:07.271
An N F T on the XRP Ledger is a one-of-a-kind token: art, a ticket, a deed or a membership.

2
00:00:07.271 --> 00:00:11.025
Owning one does not mean its issuer is done with it.

3
00:00:12.725 --> 00:00:20.118
Each N F T has a sixty-four character ID, and the rules its issuer set at minting are written inside that ID.

4
00:00:20.118 --> 00:00:25.205
NOSHASHI's Token Rights screen decodes them without even asking the ledger.

5
00:00:26.905 --> 00:00:30.916
Burnable means the issuer can destroy the token, even while you own it.

6
00:00:31.366 --> 00:00:35.057
If it is not transferable, you can only sell it back to the issuer.

7
00:00:35.507 --> 00:00:41.800
Mutable means the issuer can change what it points to, so the picture or document can change after you buy it.

8
00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:46.218
And the transfer fee lets the issuer take up to half of every resale.

9
00:00:47.918 --> 00:00:51.869
Here are two real tokens from mainnet, decoded from their IDs.

10
00:00:51.869 --> 00:00:57.795
The first can be resold, cannot be changed, and pays its issuer five percent of every resale.

11
00:00:58.245 --> 00:01:04.994
The second is mutable: its issuer can change what it points to, and it takes ten percent of every resale.

12
00:01:04.994 --> 00:01:08.272
Both labs in the Academy use these same two tokens.
